# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 4C - generated report / experiment corpus (untracked noise)
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Experiment-state directories and submission folders: generated archives and
# third-party submission bundles, never source. Ignoring them prevents an
# accidental `git add -A` (Discovery 4 hazard) and removes them from status.
evaluation/
report_archive/
.freebuff/
DiamondAI_Submission/
Nexan_Submission/
# Volatile per-batch verification reports and the full-project analysis dump.
MAYA_FULL_PROJECT_ANALYSIS.txt
MAYA_BATCH_*.md
MAYA_PRE_8J_*
MAYA_ARCHITECTURE_INTEGRITY_REPORT.md
MAYA_ASYNC_ORCHESTRATION_REPORT.md
MAYA_BRIDGE_UPDATE_COALESCING_REPORT.md
MAYA_CHAT_SUBPROCESS_REPORT.md
MAYA_OUTPUT_SUPERVISION_REGISTRATION_REPORT.md
MAYA_PERFORMANCE_INSTRUMENTATION_BASELINE_REPORT.md
MAYA_STANDING_ADDENDUM.md

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Phase 4C - volatile runtime-state JSON policy
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# These ROOT-LEVEL files are written by the application/suite runtimes on
# every launch (task queue, learning-proposal queue, presence/learning
# status, onboarding, opportunity bookmarks). They are generated state, not
# source. Policy: they REMAIN TRACKED in the working tree (status noise from
# them is expected and unchanged by this rule set); the entries below (i)
# block an accidental `git add -A` from staging fresh copies and (ii) pin the
# policy so the untrack/canonicalize decision is left to Candidate D2.
# Curated source/configuration JSON (maya_identity config trees, approval and
# scope registries, persona assets) is intentionally NOT ignored.
tasks.json
maya_learning_proposals.json
learning_status.json
presence_status.json
onboarding_pending.json
maya_opportunity_bookmarks.json
